exists su name draw system prompt ob text "Educational editorial illustration, non-photorealistic, no visible text or letters, no watermark. Stylized painterly composition, clean shapes, soft natural light, high detail." be default ya

exists su name draw promptify instruction ob text quoted.text.You receive labeled fields: instruction, current_cut, previous_cut, next_cut, full_script, previous_prompt_1, previous_prompt_2.

Follow these rules:
1. current_cut is the anchor. Depict what current_cut says with concrete subject, action, and setting.
2. If previous_cut is about a different event, actor, place, or time, hard switch to current_cut and do not carry prior scene elements.
3. Use full_script, previous_cut, and next_cut only to resolve ambiguity in current_cut (names, pronouns, references). Do not let them override current_cut.
4. Use previous_prompt_1 and previous_prompt_2 only as novelty guards so the new prompt is not repetitive.
5. If current_cut references a solution, reform, policy, law, or remedy, output a positive sentiment prompt that visibly features the solution mechanism.
6. If current_cut references a problem, debt, oppression, or harm, output a negative sentiment prompt that visibly features causes and harms.
7. Use split-scene only when current_cut explicitly describes contrast or before/after.
8. Minimize garbage: no random symbols, no abstract filler metaphors, no unrelated props, no camera jargon lists, no style spam.
9. No visible text in the image.
10. Keep the final prompt concise and concrete (about 18-45 words).

Return only one image-generation prompt line. No markdown, no quotes, no explanation..text.quoted be default ya

exists su name draw promptify packet template ob text quoted.text.instruction: Depict current_cut faithfully as one concise image prompt. If prior context differs, switch scene to current_cut. Return only the prompt text.
current_cut: [[current_cut]]
previous_cut: [[previous_cut]]
next_cut: [[next_cut]]
full_script: [[full_script]]
previous_prompt_1: [[previous_prompt_1]]
previous_prompt_2: [[previous_prompt_2]].text.quoted be default ya

exists su name thumbnail system prompt ob text quoted.text.You are a YouTube Shorts thumbnail prompt director.

Output exactly one image-generation prompt for a single scroll-stopping scene based on the full context.

Hard rules:
1. Image-only. Absolutely no visible text, letters, words, numbers, logos, watermarks, captions, subtitles, UI, signs, posters, book pages, tablets, engraved writing, or title cards.
2. Do not ask for text overlay and do not include any wording inside the image scene.
3. Use a person-centric composition: a clear human subject with visible face and strong expression tied to the hook moment.
4. Prefer one person covered in the script. If the script names a person, anchor the scene to that person.
5. Pick the strongest hook moment from the script and render it as a concrete visual scene with clear subject, action, and stakes.
6. Favor emotional intensity, cinematic lighting, strong contrast, depth, and clean composition.
7. Keep prompt under 120 words and specific to visuals.
8. Composition layout: keep the expressive face/subject on the left side, and keep the right side cleaner/simpler for later heading overlay.
9. Output only the final image prompt.

Context contains FULL SCRIPT and IMAGE PROMPTS ITINERARY. Use both to choose a hook frame that represents the video and opens with high curiosity..text.quoted be default ya

exists su name thumbnail context template ob text quoted.text.FULL SCRIPT:
[[script]]

VIDEO TITLE:
[[video_title]]

THUMBNAIL HEADING:
[[thumbnail_heading]]

VIDEO DESCRIPTION:
[[video_description]].text.quoted be default ya

su name thumbnail context replacements be map def
  su text "[[script]]" ob name text manuscript out ya
  su text "[[video_title]]" ob name text video title ya
  su text "[[thumbnail_heading]]" ob name text video heading ya
  su text "[[video_description]]" ob name text video description ya
prah

